# PRODUCTION-ONLY GATE FOR THE INTERIM LANDING PAGE
#
# Marty asked to stop the public site serving messaging that no longer matches
# where the company is. These rules send every interior page back to the
# landing page at / -- but ONLY on the live securelogicusa.com domain.
#
# securelogic.netlify.app is deliberately NOT listed, so the whole site stays
# browsable there for review while the rebuild continues.
#
# Right now this file is dormant: securelogicusa.com does not point at Netlify
# yet, so nothing matches and nothing is blocked. It switches itself on the
# moment the GoDaddy DNS is repointed. No second deploy needed.
#
# TO PUT THE FULL SITE BACK LIVE: delete this file, then move
# src/pages/home-full.astro back to src/pages/index.astro. Nothing else changes,
# because nothing was ever removed -- all 42 pages still build on every deploy.
#
# Mechanics worth knowing:
#   * A full URL in the left column is how Netlify scopes a rule to one host.
#     A bare path like /ag/* would match every domain, including netlify.app,
#     which is exactly what we are avoiding here.
#   * 302, not 301. A 301 is cached hard by browsers and would keep sending
#     people to the landing page for weeks after relaunch.
#   * The trailing ! forces the rule to win over the real page that exists at
#     that path. Without it Netlify just serves the page and never redirects.
#   * Apex and www are both listed because either may be the canonical host.
#   * /privacy-policy is intentionally absent -- legal page, no product
#     messaging, and the Facebook and Instagram profiles link to it.
#
# UNTESTABLE UNTIL THE DOMAIN IS LIVE. Host-scoped rules cannot fire locally or
# on netlify.app. Verify with the curl commands in TASKS.md after DNS cuts over.

